Patch 13: use the speed-4 DC-block-prediction level at speed 3.

Standalone. Supersedes GPT patch 0002 (which set level 1); apply INSTEAD of it.

GPT 0002 promoted dc_blk_pred_level = 1 from speed 4 to speed 3 and measured
+3.08% average speedup at +0.00% BD-rate -- a ratio near 308 against a speed-3
bar of 25, more than twelve times the required headroom. That is the largest
unclaimed margin anywhere in the current results.

Level 2 is what speed 4 already runs, so this is not a new operating point for
the encoder, only a new preset for an existing one. The difference is that
level 2 also applies DC-block prediction during winner-mode evaluation, not
only outside it.

Why this is the best remaining bet: the feature's measured BD-rate cost at
level 1 was 0.00%, and at level 2 on speed 4 it was +0.04% (ratio 77.0). Both
are far below the level at which the bar binds, so the plausible range of
outcomes is dominated by how much additional time level 2 saves rather than by
quality risk.

The honest caveat is the one this branch has now learned twice. Loosening a
comfortably-passing threshold worked for transform-partition stationarity
pruning (ratio 23.6 -> 26.7 with speedup up 54%) and then failed at the very
next step (down to 14.7). Large headroom makes a step likely to succeed, it
does not make it safe. -DAVM_S3_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL=1 restores the measured
level-1 operating point exactly, with no patch edit.

Expected direction: more speedup than 0002's +3.08%, BD-rate still small but no
longer exactly zero.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
index f363519..c0e3f38 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
@@ -555,6 +555,28 @@ static void set_good_speed_features_framesize_independent(
     // For screen content, "prune_sgr_based_on_wiener = 2" cause large quality
     // loss.
     sf->lpf_sf.disable_loop_restoration_chroma = boosted ? 0 : 1;
+
+    // Use the speed-4 DC-block predictor level at speed 3.
+    //
+    // The 101-feature study measured dc_blk_pred_level = 2 at speed 4 as one of
+    // the most efficient features in the encoder: +3.08% time for +0.04%
+    // BD-rate, ratio 77.0 against a bar of 20. Promoting the *conservative*
+    // level 1 to speed 3 then measured +3.08% for +0.00% BD-rate -- a ratio of
+    // roughly 308 against a speed-3 bar of 25, which is more than twelve times
+    // the headroom the feature is required to have.
+    //
+    // Headroom that large is unclaimed speedup. Level 2 is what speed 4 already
+    // runs, so this is not a new operating point for the encoder, only a new
+    // preset for an existing one: it additionally enables DC-block prediction
+    // during winner-mode evaluation rather than only outside it.
+    //
+    // Level 1 measured ~0.00% BD-rate, so the marginal cost of the extra
+    // prediction is the only unknown. Build with -DAVM_S3_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL=1
+    // to fall back to the measured level-1 operating point exactly.
+#ifndef AVM_S3_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL
+#define AVM_S3_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL 2
+#endif
+    sf->winner_mode_sf.dc_blk_pred_level = AVM_S3_DC_BLK_PRED_LEVEL;
   }
 
   if (speed >= 4) {
